  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "fieldStrength",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Magnetic field strength B₀ (tesla)",
      "range": [1.8, 2.6, 0.005],
      "default": 2.1,
      "teaches": "At fixed rf frequency, only one field value satisfies ν = γB₀/2π for a given nucleus, so nuclei of different shielding come into resonance one at a time as the field is swept — which is why a spectrum is a set of separate peaks rather than a single absorption."
