CONTEXT FROM TEXTBOOK:
This figure is a perspective pictorial schematic of a basic NMR spectrometer, laying out sample, magnet, and signal path in one view. At the center a slender glass tube holding an orange column of sample solution stands upright, tagged "Sample in tube" by a leader line; a green helical coil wraps the tube's midsection between two blue collars. Two cylindrical magnet pole pieces face the coil from either side, the left one lettered S and the right one lettered N. At lower left a beige benchtop unit with knobs, small colored buttons, and a green digital readout showing 9.56 is labeled "Radiofrequency generator", and green leads run from it up to the coil. Blue cables leave the coil to the right and enter a dark gray box with two dials and a green and a red pushbutton, labeled "Detector and amplifier", from which further blue cables climb to a flat-panel monitor at the upper right. The monitor shows a pale blue field crossed by a red baseline carrying several sharp vertical peaks of unequal height. The left-to-right arrangement traces energy from generator to sample to detector to display, letting the reader follow one absorption event to a plotted line. The drawing introduces the instrument in which a strong field aligns 1H and 13C nuclei and swept field strength brings each into resonance separately.

PROJECTION TYPE: perspective
Use the scaffold's true perspective projection after building all geometry. Use this only when the source has real vanishing-point convergence or distance-based size shrinkage; then depth should visibly affect apparent size.

ELEMENTS TO RECREATE IN 3D:
  - slender vertical glass sample tube (transparent, rounded bottom, open top lip) at center of scene
  - orange column of sample solution filling the lower-middle of the tube
  - green helical rf coil wrapped around the tube's midsection
  - two blue cylindrical collars capping the top and bottom of the green coil
  - left magnet pole piece: horizontal gray metal cylinder facing the coil, lettered 'S' on its circular face
  - right magnet pole piece: horizontal gray metal cylinder facing the coil, lettered 'N' on its circular face
  - beige benchtop radiofrequency generator box at lower left, drawn in slight three-quarter view
  - generator front panel: two large black knobs, a row of small colored buttons (red/blue/green/yellow), and a rectangular green LCD reading '9.56'
  - two green lead cables running from the generator up and right to the lower blue collar of the coil
  - dark gray detector and amplifier box at lower right with a lighter vertical seam panel
  - detector front panel: two small round dials, a silver knob, one green pushbutton and one red pushbutton
  - two blue cables running right from the coil's lower collar into the left side of the detector box
  - two blue cables rising from the detector top to the back-left of the monitor
  - flat-panel monitor at upper right: dark bezel, pedestal neck and oval base
  - monitor screen: pale blue field with a horizontal red baseline and several sharp vertical black/red peaks of unequal height
  - leader line and text label 'Sample in tube' pointing to the upper tube
  - text labels 'Radiofrequency generator', 'Detector and amplifier'
  - invisible magnetic field axis between S and N poles (revealed on demand as field lines / arrows)
  - nuclear spin markers inside the orange sample volume (small arrows that flip at resonance)

GEOMETRY NOTES (world-space scale, color palette, and any formula/value needed for correctness — build to these so sizes, zoom, and colors match the source; do not guess dimensions the notes already specify):
Scene spans roughly x ∈ [-9, 9], y ∈ [-5, 5], z ∈ [-3, 3] world units; ground plane is y = -4.

CENTER — SAMPLE ASSEMBLY (at origin, x=0,z=0): glass tube is a vertical cylinder radius 0.35, height 7.0, centered at y=0 (so top y=+3.5, bottom y=-3.5), rounded hemispherical bottom cap, thin open lip at top; material transparent pale blue-white (#cfe8f5, opacity ~0.35, slight blue rim). Orange sample column inside: cylinder radius 0.28 extending y = -3.2 up to y = +2.3, gradient orange #E8A33D → #D97B22. Green rf coil: helix of tube radius 0.07 coiled at radius 0.55 around the tube, from y = -1.6 to y = +1.6, ~26 turns, color #3FA845 with darker windings. Two blue collars: cylinders radius 0.62, height 0.5, centered at y = +1.85 and y = -1.85, color #1C6FC4 with lighter highlight band.

MAGNET POLES: two horizontal gray cylinders on the ±X axis, axis along X, radius 1.5, length 2.6. Left (S) pole occupies x from -3.8 to -1.2, right (N) pole x from +1.2 to +3.8, both centered at y = -0.1, z = 0. They do NOT touch the coil (gap of ~0.6 from coil outer radius). Metal gray with vertical gradient highlight (#DCDDE0 top → #8A8C90 bottom, bright specular band across the middle). Letter 'S' in bold black on the flat face of the left cylinder facing right (the inner face at x = -1.2), letter 'N' on the inner face of the right cylinder at x = +1.2 — both letters read upright and face the viewer-right/center of the image.

RADIOFREQUENCY GENERATOR: beige box at lower left, centered near (-6.2, -3.2, 1.6), dimensions 4.2 (X) × 1.5 (Y) × 2.6 (Z), sloped front face tilted ~20° toward viewer. Body #E8DCC0 / #D8CBA8 with a darker beige lower strip. On the sloped top face: green LCD panel 1.6 × 0.7 (#7FCB7F background, dark green seven-segment '9.56'), two black round knobs radius 0.22 to the left of it, and a 3×2 grid of small colored button dots (red, blue, green, yellow, #E03030 / #3070D0 / #30A050) at the far left. Front lower strip carries 4 small black rocker switches and one red indicator. Two green cables (#3FA845, tube radius 0.05) leave the generator's top-right corner, run as parallel bezier curves right and slightly up, and terminate on the BOTTOM blue collar at (0, -1.85, 0) — they approach from the lower-left.

DETECTOR AND AMPLIFIER: dark gray box at lower right, centered near (5.0, -2.6, 1.2), dimensions 2.2 (X) × 3.0 (Y) × 2.2 (Z), standing upright like a tower; a lighter gray vertical seam panel splits the front face into a narrow left strip and wider right face. Body #3A3D42 with #565A60 highlights. Front detail: two small round dials radius 0.15 near the top (one on each panel), a silver knob radius 0.18 below the left dial, a green pushbutton (#2E9E4F) and a red pushbutton (#C43434) radius 0.22 side by side near the bottom. Two blue cables (#2AA8E0, radius 0.05) leave the bottom blue collar region at (0.6, -1.9, 0), run right and gently down, and enter the detector's left face. Two more blue cables leave the detector's top face, rise up and right, and enter the back-left of the monitor.

MONITOR: flat panel at upper right, screen plane centered near (7.2, 1.9, -0.3), rotated ~-25° about Y so it faces left toward the viewer. Bezel 4.6 (W) × 3.2 (H) × 0.28 (D), color #2B2E31 with a soft gray gradient on the top edge. Inset screen 4.1 × 2.6, pale blue #A8D8EF. Inside the screen: horizontal red baseline (#D93A2B, thickness 0.05) at ~35% up from the screen bottom, spanning the full width. Peaks rise from the baseline as thin vertical dark-red/black lines: a cluster of 3 short peaks at 22–32% of the screen width (heights 0.35, 0.55, 0.30 of available headroom) and 2 tall peaks at 72% and 80% (heights 1.0 and 0.75). Pedestal: short neck 0.5 × 0.6 × 0.4 plus an elliptical base 1.8 × 0.15 × 0.9 in dark gray.

LABELS (billboarded dark text, ~0.45 world units tall, serif/sans as in source): 'Sample in tube' at upper left around (-4.6, 3.2, 0) with a thin black leader line angling down-right to the glass tube at (-0.3, 2.4, 0). 'Radiofrequency generator' at (-8.0, -0.6, 0), two lines, left-aligned. 'Detector and amplifier' at (6.4, -3.6, 0), two lines.

PHYSICS: resonance condition ν = γB₀/2π. Hold ν fixed at 9.56 (displayed, arbitrary units matching the source readout). Map the slider range B₀ = 1.8–2.6 T onto the spectrum's horizontal axis, left edge = 1.8 T (downfield/deshielded) to right edge = 2.6 T (upfield/shielded). Assign the five peaks resonance fields of 2.02, 2.06, 2.10, 2.38 and 2.44 T with relative intensities 0.35, 0.55, 0.30, 1.0, 0.75. When |B₀ − B_peak| < 0.02 T, the corresponding peak brightens/grows and the spin arrows inside the orange sample flash white and flip 180°; otherwise spins point uniformly up along +X (parallel to the pole axis).

